1
00:00:00,930 --> 00:00:08,480
B1 Daniel is listening to a talk on how to stay safe in natural disasters.

2
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:13,235
Listen with him and complete the notes below.

3
00:00:13,235 --> 00:00:21,000
Hello everybody, today I'd like to give you some advice on dealing with natural disasters.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,910
If there's a flood, you should get to high ground and stay there.

5
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:31,560
Don't get close to or even walk through the water as it may wash you away.

6
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:37,950
If you are caught in a typhoon, you must quickly go inside the nearest building.

7
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:45,790
The strong winds can move cars and other big objects, so it is very dangerous to be outside.

8
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:51,290
When an earthquake happens, you should get outside as soon as possible.

9
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:57,550
However, if you can't, stay under a strong desk or table to protect yourself.

10
00:00:57,550 --> 00:01:02,230
Don't stand near a window because you may get hurt.

11
00:01:02,230 --> 00:01:04,740
That's all for today's talk.

12
00:01:04,740 --> 00:01:08,920
I hope you know more about how to keep yourself safe and sound.
